---
description: Supabase backend and client integration contracts
globs:
  - "supabase/**/*"
  - "src/lib/supabase*"
  - "src/lib/supabase/**/*"
  - "src/features/**/api.ts"
  - "src/features/**/api/**/*.ts"
  - "src/features/auth/*api*.ts"
  - "src/features/auth/AuthProvider*.tsx"
  - "src/features/auth/hooks.ts"
  - "src/types/database.generated.ts"
---

Select references by effect:
- Schema, SQL, RLS, grants or database functions: affected `docs/DATA_MODEL.md`
  and `docs/API_CONTRACTS.md`; `skills/supabase-schema-change/SKILL.md`.
- Existing-schema client reads or data mappings: affected `docs/API_CONTRACTS.md`;
  no schema workflow merely because the client uses Supabase.
- Auth/session, private data, server boundaries or environment actions:
  affected `docs/SECURITY.md` and API contract; integration remains parent-owned.

Never expose a service-role key in the client. Production database access and
actual agent-executed account deletion are forbidden. Seed-only work does not
select schema implementation unless it changes a database contract.

The globs cover backend and client integration paths. Pure frontend helpers and
presentation do not select this rule; use the same owners when an out-of-glob
change affects a protected contract.
